  body: "# Couple in Pension Credit guidance\n\n**Model-assisted source interpretation; unreviewed. No
    entitlement decision or executable rule.**\n\nThe captured definition distinguishes spouses or civil
    partners in the same household from people living together as if they were married or civil partners.\n\
    \n## Evidence and scope\n\n[DMG 77013, PDF page 7](https://assets.publishing.service.gov.uk/media/68401a731d85c6606009cce4/dmgch77.pdf#page=7)
    supports this scoped proposal. The source PDF SHA-256 is `0528f2fb95ac3bd71bdff0d91cdaba5df76ab4260396ca99608c840004ff5708`.\n\
    \nDo not import this definition into Universal Credit or infer the claimant's household membership
    from marital status alone.\n\nThe capture date, the publication page's update date and a date stated
    in the guidance have different meanings. Linked legislation and memos need their own provision, version
    and applicability review.\n"
  semantic_relations:
  - target: term/household
    predicate: http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#related
    rationale: The household element belongs to the captured Pension Credit couple definition; this
      is a scoped association, not a universal household definition.
    evidence:
    - page: page/77/0007
      quote: "77013 Couple means1\n\n\n1. two people who are married to, or civil partners of, each other
        and are members of the same\nhousehold; or\n\n\n2. two people who are not married to, or civil
        partners of, each other but are living together as if they\nwere a married couple or civil partners.\n\
        \n\n                                                                                         \
        \   1 SPC Regs Reg 1(2)"
      locator: DMG 77013
